sharepoint-add-list-column|Add SharePoint List Column|spo-add-list-column.ps1|ADD-SPO-LIST-COLUMN|Adds a column directly to an existing SharePoint list or library. Use when a column belongs to one list only. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token ADD-SPO-LIST-COLUMN.|Add a column to one existing list or library with Add-PnPField.|The target list or library must already exist; this adds a column, not a list.|The dry-run summary lists the column(s) and the target list; afterwards the column exists on that list.
sharepoint-add-list-item|Add SharePoint List Items|spo-add-list-item.ps1|ADD-SPO-LIST-ITEM|Creates new list items in a SharePoint list with given field values. Use to seed or load items into an existing list. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token ADD-SPO-LIST-ITEM.|Create items in an existing list with Add-PnPListItem.|Creates items only; it does not create the list or its columns. Use only field values the plan supplies.|The dry-run summary lists the items; afterwards the items exist with the supplied values.
sharepoint-configure-column-formatting|Configure SharePoint Column Formatting|spo-configure-column-formatting.ps1|CONFIGURE-SPO-COLUMN-FORMATTING|Applies JSON custom column formatting and custom renderers to SharePoint fields. Use to change how a column displays. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token CONFIGURE-SPO-COLUMN-FORMATTING.|Apply JSON column formatting (CustomFormatter) to fields.|Apply the formatting JSON the plan supplies; do not author or alter it.|The dry-run summary names the fields; afterwards each column renders with its formatter.
sharepoint-configure-library-settings|Configure SharePoint Library Settings|spo-configure-library-settings.ps1|CONFIGURE-SPO-LIBRARY-SETTINGS|Configures advanced SharePoint document library version limits, content approval and draft visibility settings. Use to tune versioning and approval on a library. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token CONFIGURE-SPO-LIBRARY-SETTINGS.|Set library version limits, content approval and draft visibility with Set-PnPList.|Limited to version limits, content approval and draft visibility; use sharepoint-update-list-settings for a list's title, description or general versioning.|The dry-run summary lists the settings; afterwards the library reports them.
sharepoint-create-content-type|Create SharePoint Content Type|spo-provision-content-types.ps1|PROVISION-SPO-CONTENT-TYPES|Creates new SharePoint content types, binds field links and attaches content types to target lists. Use to define a reusable content type. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token PROVISION-SPO-CONTENT-TYPES.|Create content types, bind field links and attach them to lists in one plan.|Check that the site columns the plan references exist before a real run (create them with sharepoint-create-site-column first).|The dry-run summary lists the content types, field links and target lists; afterwards the content type exists and is attached.
sharepoint-create-document-library|Create SharePoint Document Library|spo-provision-list.ps1|PROVISION-SPO-LIST|Creates a new SharePoint document library (Template 101) using PnP.PowerShell. Use to add a document library to a site. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token PROVISION-SPO-LIST.|Create a document library (Template 101) with New-PnPList.|Shares spo-provision-list.ps1 with sharepoint-create-list and sharepoint-remove-list, which applies a duplicate-title gate on the plan's blocking_findings.|The dry-run summary lists the library; afterwards a Get-PnPList re-check finds it.
sharepoint-create-list|Create SharePoint List|spo-provision-list.ps1|PROVISION-SPO-LIST|Creates a new SharePoint custom list (Template 100) using PnP.PowerShell. Use to add a custom list to a site. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token PROVISION-SPO-LIST.|Create a custom list (Template 100) with New-PnPList.|Shares spo-provision-list.ps1 with sharepoint-create-document-library and sharepoint-remove-list, which applies a duplicate-title gate on the plan's blocking_findings. A generic list gets a default Title column with Required set to true (see the contract reference).|The dry-run summary lists the list; afterwards a Get-PnPList re-check finds it.
sharepoint-create-list-view|Create SharePoint List View|spo-provision-list-view.ps1|PROVISION-SPO-LIST-VIEW|Creates and configures custom views for SharePoint lists and document libraries. Use to add a filtered or sorted view. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token PROVISION-SPO-LIST-VIEW.|Create and configure a custom view with Add-PnPView.|A view references columns; confirm they exist on the list before a real run.|The dry-run summary lists the view and its columns; afterwards the view exists on the list.
sharepoint-create-site-column|Create SharePoint Site Column|spo-provision-site-columns.ps1|PROVISION-SPO-SITE-COLUMNS|Creates new SharePoint site columns across standard or complex types (Text, Choice, Lookup, User, Calculated via Field XML). Use to define a reusable site column. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token PROVISION-SPO-SITE-COLUMNS.|Create site columns with Add-PnPField, or Add-PnPFieldFromXml for complex types.|Supports standard and complex types, including Calculated via Field XML; use Field XML as supplied and do not rewrite formulas.|The dry-run summary lists each column and type; afterwards the site column exists.
sharepoint-detach-content-type|Detach SharePoint Content Type|spo-detach-content-type-from-list.ps1|DETACH-SPO-CONTENT-TYPE|Detaches and unlinks a content type from a specific SharePoint list or library. Use to stop a list using a content type without deleting it. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token DETACH-SPO-CONTENT-TYPE.|Unlink a content type from one list with Remove-PnPContentTypeFromList.|Detaches from one list only; the site content type stays. Use sharepoint-remove-content-type to delete it from the site collection.|The dry-run summary names the list and content type; afterwards the list no longer offers the content type.
sharepoint-remove-content-type|Remove SharePoint Content Type|spo-remove-content-type.ps1|REMOVE-SPO-CONTENT-TYPES|Deletes a SharePoint content type from the site collection. Use to remove an obsolete content type. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token REMOVE-SPO-CONTENT-TYPES.|Delete a content type from the site collection with Remove-PnPContentType.|Destructive. The script does not check whether the content type is still in use; detach it from lists first (sharepoint-detach-content-type) and confirm there are no dependents.|The dry-run summary names the content type; afterwards it no longer exists in the site collection.
sharepoint-remove-list|Remove SharePoint List|spo-provision-list.ps1|PROVISION-SPO-LIST|Deletes a SharePoint list or document library and re-checks that it is gone, failing loud if it still exists. Use to remove an obsolete list or library. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token PROVISION-SPO-LIST.|Delete a list or library with Remove-PnPList -Force.|Destructive. After deleting, the script re-checks with Get-PnPList and fails loud if the list still exists; never report an unverified delete as success. The duplicate-title gate on the plan's blocking_findings applies.|The dry-run summary names the list; after a real run the re-check finds it gone.
sharepoint-remove-list-column|Remove SharePoint List Column|spo-remove-list-column.ps1|REMOVE-SPO-LIST-COLUMN|Removes a list-scoped column from a SharePoint list or library. Use to drop a column from one list only. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token REMOVE-SPO-LIST-COLUMN.|Remove a list-scoped column with Remove-PnPField.|Destructive for that column's data on that list only; remove a site column with sharepoint-remove-site-column instead. The script does not check whether the column is in use.|The dry-run summary names the list and column; afterwards the column is gone from that list.
sharepoint-remove-site-column|Remove SharePoint Site Column|spo-remove-site-column.ps1|REMOVE-SPO-SITE-COLUMNS|Deletes a SharePoint site column and reports each column as removed or failed. Use to remove an obsolete site column. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token REMOVE-SPO-SITE-COLUMNS.|Delete site columns with Remove-PnPField -Force.|Destructive and site-wide. The script does not check dependents and does not re-check afterwards (it records each column as removed or failed); confirm no content types or lists use the column and verify it is gone.|The result lists each column under removed or failed with an outcome of OBSERVED, PARTIAL or FAILED.
sharepoint-update-content-type|Update SharePoint Content Type|spo-update-content-type.ps1|UPDATE-SPO-CONTENT-TYPES|Updates SharePoint content type name, description, group or hidden properties. Use to rename or reclassify a content type. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token UPDATE-SPO-CONTENT-TYPES.|Change a content type's name, description, group or hidden flag with Set-PnPContentType.|Changes name, description, group and hidden only; adding or removing field links is sharepoint-create-content-type's job.|The dry-run summary shows each property change; afterwards the content type carries the new values.
sharepoint-update-list-column|Update SharePoint List Column|spo-update-list-column.ps1|UPDATE-SPO-LIST-COLUMN|Updates a list-scoped column's properties on a specific SharePoint list. Use to change one list's column. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token UPDATE-SPO-LIST-COLUMN.|Update a list-scoped column with Set-PnPField.|List-scoped: changes one list's column only. Treat a column type change as risky and confirm it with the user.|The dry-run summary shows each property change; afterwards that list's column carries the new values.
sharepoint-update-list-settings|Update SharePoint List Settings|spo-update-list.ps1|UPDATE-SPO-LIST|Updates SharePoint list or library title, description and versioning settings using Set-PnPList. Use to rename or reconfigure a list. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token UPDATE-SPO-LIST.|Change a list's title, description and versioning with Set-PnPList.|Title, description and versioning only. To recreate a list use sharepoint-remove-list then sharepoint-create-list; to tune approval and draft visibility use sharepoint-configure-library-settings.|The dry-run summary shows each setting change; afterwards the list reports the new values.
sharepoint-update-site-column|Update SharePoint Site Column|spo-update-site-column.ps1|UPDATE-SPO-SITE-COLUMNS|Updates existing SharePoint site column properties (display name, description, required, choices) using Set-PnPField. Use to change a reusable site column. Dry-run by default; real writes require -Execute and confirmation token UPDATE-SPO-SITE-COLUMNS.|Update a site column's display name, description, required flag and choices with Set-PnPField.|Changes the site column everywhere it is used. Removing a choice can affect items that already use it; confirm with the user.|The dry-run summary shows each property change; afterwards the site column carries the new values.
